# Mahbere Ahaw Seminary LMS

Read and obey `.ai/agent.md`, `.ai/rules.md`, `.ai/best-practices.md`, and `.ai/grill-me.md`.

## Priorities

Maintainability → Scalability → Security → Readability → Performance

Never optimize for development speed at the expense of architecture.

## Stack

- Frontend: Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, TanStack Query, Zustand, RHF, Zod
- Backend: NestJS, Prisma, PostgreSQL 17, Redis, BullMQ, JWT + refresh, Argon2, MinIO
- Real-time: WebSocket notifications (queued via BullMQ, never sync)

## Architecture

Modular monolith. Each feature owns controller, service, repository, dto, validation, tests.

- Controllers thin; business logic in services; DB in repositories
- No `any`; never disable TypeScript
- No hardcoded IDs, URLs, roles, or permissions
- Every endpoint validates input + authorization
- DB changes via Prisma migrations only
- Soft delete; UUID PKs; consistent API responses

## Domain constraints

- Drip unlock: Month N opens 30 days after student `cohortStartedAt` (Month 1 immediate)
- Offline reading after download; online required for submit + new downloads
- Files in object storage only — never in PostgreSQL

